    "reply": "The graph links NCBIGene:672 and NCBIGene:675 to a set of inherited cancer-predisposition and DNA-repair disorders. For NCBIGene:672, BRCA1 DNA repair associated, the associated conditions are listed below [1].\n\nFamilial cancer of breast [2].\n\nFamilial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [3].\n\nPancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [4].\n\nFanconi anemia complementation group S [5].\n\n## BRCA2 Associated Conditions\n\nNCBIGene:675 is BRCA2 DNA repair associated [6]. Its associated conditions are listed below.\n\nMedulloblastoma [7].\n\nFanconi anemia complementation group D1 [8].\n\nFamilial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 2 [9].\n\nGlioma susceptibility 3 [10].\n\nFamilial prostate cancer [11].\n\nPancreatic cancer susceptibility 2 [12].\n\nWilms tumor 1 [13].\n\n## Biological Basis\n\nThe BRCA1 product helps maintain genome integrity and functions as a tumor suppressor [24: \"plays a role in maintaining genomic stability, and it also acts as a tumor suppressor\"]. It participates in transcription, double-strand break repair and recombination [24: \"plays a role in transcription, DNA repair of double-stranded breaks, and recombination\"]. It is annotated to GO:0000724, double-strand break repair via homologous recombination [21].\n\n## Clinical Relevance\n\nBRCA1 mutations explain a large share of hereditary breast and breast-ovarian cancer [24: \"responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers\"]. A related registered study is Germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 Mutations in Jewish Women Affected by Breast Cancer [19].",
